    "proseDraft": "No confirmed resolutions are listed. The stated remarks covered Wednesday submission, the usual QA pass, drafts, and onboarding screens. Still open are the reading of QA completion and submission timing and the scope of skipping onboarding this round.\n\nUnresolved\n- It is still open with a failed recheck how to read QA as done when full manual regression passes on the eight lab devices and accessibility checklist passes on the compose screen with submission moving to Thursday 2026-10-29.\n- It is still open how to read the scope of Zara skipping onboarding this round.\n\nStated in the meeting\n- Someone said to submit Wednesday if the usual QA pass is clean.\n- Someone said Wednesday works.\n- Someone said the usual QA pass will be done on the release build.\n- Someone said they will draft them from the changelog and send them.\n- Someone said to keep them short at three bullets at most.\n- Someone asked about mentioning the rotation fix because store reviews complained about it.\n- Someone said yes to lead with that.\n- Someone said the new onboarding screens are behind a flag and ship dark.\n- Someone said they will be turned on once the A/B setup is ready.\n- Someone said they will skip onboarding this round."
